  "body": [
    {
      "_key": "000000000001",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "000000000000",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "Egypt isn't a country that fits one vacation style."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "000000000003",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "qhya3vulb9d1",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "It can be an archaeology trip touring pyramids and the "
        },
        {
          "_key": "k85mi5bgw32f",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [
            "8egt2m7qlc1i"
          ],
          "text": "Valley of the Kings"
        },
        {
          "_key": "xlxkl87quqvx",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": ". A city trip walking "
        },
        {
          "_key": "dgxu6zofheco",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [
            "5bxfl89utf7v"
          ],
          "text": "Cairo"
        },
        {
          "_key": "jgd9dtv6i3to",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": ". A resort vacation swimming in the Red Sea doing nothing. A landscape trip heading to the White Desert or Siwa."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [
        {
          "_key": "8egt2m7qlc1i",
          "_type": "internalLink",
          "reference": {
            "_ref": "guideArticle.luxor.valley-of-the-kings",
            "_type": "reference"
          }
        },
        {
          "_key": "5bxfl89utf7v",
          "_type": "internalLink",
          "reference": {
            "_ref": "wp-page-83284",
            "_type": "reference"
          }
        }
      ],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "000000000005",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "000000000004",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "So what to decide first thinking about Egypt isn't only \"where to go.\""
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "000000000007",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "000000000006",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "What kind of vacation you want."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "000000000009",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "000000000008",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "A trip centred on Nile sites"
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "h2"
    },
    {
      "_key": "00000000000b",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "00000000000a",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "To see ancient Egypt, the trip's centre becomes the Nile valley."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "00000000000d",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "3t4rffizqet0",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "In Cairo and "
        },
        {
          "_key": "6e7w7an0d03h",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [
            "m7ja77vony8t"
          ],
          "text": "Giza"
        },
        {
          "_key": "679sdg26ympa",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": ", visit pyramids, Great Sphinx, and the Grand Egyptian Museum. The Giza pyramids symbolise Old Kingdom royal power; GEM is a large-scale ancient Egyptian entry including Tutankhamun displays."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [
        {
          "_key": "m7ja77vony8t",
          "_type": "internalLink",
          "reference": {
            "_ref": "wp-page-58854",
            "_type": "reference"
          }
        }
      ],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "00000000000f",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "klihcje3dkse",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [
            "omsbw8emwfeo"
          ],
          "text": "Luxor"
        },
        {
          "_key": "afn6fx354lkm",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": " is the city where you feel ancient Egypt most deeply. East bank — Karnak and "
        },
        {
          "_key": "ctpkrq3iai8l",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [
            "lxj0pfrndhvs"
          ],
          "text": "Luxor Temple"
        },
        {
          "_key": "nnk6avaibbrp",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": ". West bank — Valley of the Kings, "
        },
        {
          "_key": "uyhjkkiivx1o",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [
            "knvz5i93b1tw"
          ],
          "text": "Valley of the Queens"
        },
        {
          "_key": "o7fffs2jxdpa",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": ", Hatshepsut, "
        },
        {
          "_key": "qlpervmmgmhx",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [
            "l546rcvdyhq7"
          ],
          "text": "Medinet Habu"
        },
        {
          "_key": "bdkz7r9s8xvo",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": ", "
        },
        {
          "_key": "6ald2xoozt5d",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [
            "znjv9f3i0ui0"
          ],
          "text": "Deir el-Medina"
        },
        {
          "_key": "5ildxygofvaq",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [
        {
          "_key": "omsbw8emwfeo",
          "_type": "internalLink",
          "reference": {
            "_ref": "wp-page-58877",
            "_type": "reference"
          }
        },
        {
          "_key": "lxj0pfrndhvs",
          "_type": "internalLink",
          "reference": {
            "_ref": "guideArticle.luxor.the-luxor-temple",
            "_type": "reference"
          }
        },
        {
          "_key": "knvz5i93b1tw",
          "_type": "internalLink",
          "reference": {
            "_ref": "guideArticle.luxor.valley-of-the-queens",
            "_type": "reference"
          }
        },
        {
          "_key": "l546rcvdyhq7",
          "_type": "internalLink",
          "reference": {
            "_ref": "guideArticle.luxor.madinat-habu-temple",
            "_type": "reference"
          }
        },
        {
          "_key": "znjv9f3i0ui0",
          "_type": "internalLink",
          "reference": {
            "_ref": "guideArticle.luxor.deir-el-madina",
            "_type": "reference"
          }
        }
      ],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "000000000011",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "ihx6x0ikpxak",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "In "
        },
        {
          "_key": "x71fy1pfthvs",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [
            "5j8xaczqst8c"
          ],
          "text": "Aswan"
        },
        {
          "_key": "eq1xrmk2gb58",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": ", you see Philae, "
        },
        {
          "_key": "0bp9j3lpiv0m",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [
            "5ljmzqo1ph8s"
          ],
          "text": "the Unfinished Obelisk"
        },
        {
          "_key": "geyqnwj8r7zu",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": ", Nubian Museum, and Nile islands. Further south, "
        },
        {
          "_key": "yu6000io40us",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [
            "btv5ga6of0oz"
          ],
          "text": "Abu Simbel"
        },
        {
          "_key": "ckk8muat0nq4",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": " also becomes a candidate."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [
        {
          "_key": "5j8xaczqst8c",
          "_type": "internalLink",
          "reference": {
            "_ref": "wp-page-58758",
            "_type": "reference"
          }
        },
        {
          "_key": "5ljmzqo1ph8s",
          "_type": "internalLink",
          "reference": {
            "_ref": "guideArticle.aswan.the-unfinished-obelisk",
            "_type": "reference"
          }
        },
        {
          "_key": "btv5ga6of0oz",
          "_type": "internalLink",
          "reference": {
            "_ref": "wp-page-56813",
            "_type": "reference"
          }
        }
      ],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "000000000013",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "000000000012",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "For first archaeology-centred vacations, Cairo, Luxor, and Aswan as axis is most natural. With limited days, narrowing to Cairo and Luxor reduces transfer fatigue."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "000000000015",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "000000000014",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "A trip seeing Cairo properly"
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "h2"
    },
    {
      "_key": "000000000017",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "000000000016",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "Cairo isn't just a transit to the pyramids."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "000000000019",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "xqw2juxknfu7",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "Islamic Cairo, Coptic district, "
        },
        {
          "_key": "zefdkcnfozw9",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [
            "fq2h2c9r25th"
          ],
          "text": "Khan el-Khalili"
        },
        {
          "_key": "354jbyosu8ge",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": ", Citadel, Nile-side, modern cafés and restaurants, museums. Cairo holds history and city life beyond ancient Egypt."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [
        {
          "_key": "fq2h2c9r25th",
          "_type": "internalLink",
          "reference": {
            "_ref": "guideArticle.cairo.khan-el-khalili",
            "_type": "reference"
          }
        }
      ],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "00000000001b",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "00000000001a",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "Around al-Muizz Street, Fatimid, Mamluk, and Ottoman architecture layer. Ibn Tulun Mosque, Sultan Hasan Mosque, around al-Azhar, and old commercial buildings show Cairo was an important medieval Islamic-world city."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "00000000001d",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "7trn723fehif",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "In the Coptic district, through "
        },
        {
          "_key": "3zzpc24ragzu",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [
            "ji50t67iu1kn"
          ],
          "text": "the Hanging Church"
        },
        {
          "_key": "hbz2d67u9s7p",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": ", Church of Saints Sergius and Bacchus, and "
        },
        {
          "_key": "gfi0l4dk3wja",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [
            "mfof9d62t2m4"
          ],
          "text": "Ben Ezra Synagogue"
        },
        {
          "_key": "30icy18k54qw",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": ", you can touch Christian and Jewish history too."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [
        {
          "_key": "ji50t67iu1kn",
          "_type": "internalLink",
          "reference": {
            "_ref": "guideArticle.cairo.the-hanging-church",
            "_type": "reference"
          }
        },
        {
          "_key": "mfof9d62t2m4",
          "_type": "internalLink",
          "reference": {
            "_ref": "guideArticle.cairo.ben-ezra-synagogue",
            "_type": "reference"
          }
        }
      ],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "00000000001f",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "00000000001e",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "Rushing Cairo in one day misses this layer mostly. With city interest, beyond pyramids and museum, at least one day on the city itself has value."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "000000000021",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "000000000020",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "A trip resting on the Red Sea"
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "h2"
    },
    {
      "_key": "000000000023",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "000000000022",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "Weighing vacation feel, the Red Sea is a strong choice."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "000000000025",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "000000000024",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "In Hurghada, Sharm el-Sheikh, Marsa Alam, and Dahab, you spend on sea, pool, snorkelling, diving, and resort stay. A completely different Egypt from Nile-valley sites."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "000000000027",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "000000000026",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "Hurghada combines easily with Cairo and Luxor, suiting family travel and resort stay. Sharm el-Sheikh has Ras Mohammed and Strait of Tiran access, popular for diving and snorkelling. Dahab is smaller, with relaxed seaside town atmosphere."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "000000000029",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "000000000028",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "If including Red Sea, placing at the trip's end works well. After walking Cairo and Luxor, several seaside days keep the whole trip from getting too heavy."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "00000000002b",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "00000000002a",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "Forcing Red Sea into short itineraries cuts site time. Whether vacation purpose is sea or ancient sites — decide first."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "00000000002d",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "00000000002c",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "A trip of desert and oasis"
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "h2"
    },
    {
      "_key": "00000000002f",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "00000000002e",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "Egypt has not only Nile and Red Sea but desert travel."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "000000000031",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "000000000030",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "White Desert spreads wind-carved white limestone landform. Night desert, stars, morning light leave strong impressions different from temples or museums."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "000000000033",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "000000000032",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "Siwa Oasis is in the Western Desert near the Libyan border. Salt lakes, palm groves, springs, old mud-salt architecture, the Oracle of Amun, and Amazigh culture show a completely different Egypt from the Nile valley."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "000000000035",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "000000000034",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "Bahariya, Farafra, Dakhla, and Kharga oases relate to desert roads and caravan history too."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "000000000037",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "000000000036",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "Desert travel needs preparation. Road conditions, permits, local safety judgment, and trusted vehicle and guide matter. For first short vacations, sometimes not forcing desert in is better; consider on returners or longer trips."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "000000000039",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "000000000038",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "Nile cruise or dahabiya"
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "h2"
    },
    {
      "_key": "00000000003b",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "00000000003a",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "Moving between Luxor and Aswan, many consider Nile cruise or dahabiya."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "00000000003d",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "00000000003c",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "Large Nile cruise combines transfer, lodging, food, and sightseeing, clear for first travellers. Stopping at Edfu, Kom Ombo, and Esna while moving the river."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "00000000003f",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "00000000003e",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "Dahabiya is a smaller, quieter sailing-type trip. Fewer passengers, more time tasting the river itself. Suits those weighing quiet, small-group, and Nile scenery over large facilities or entertainment."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "000000000041",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "000000000040",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "Which is better depends on trip purpose. Weighing efficiency and reassurance — large cruise. Wanting slow river travel — dahabiya. Choosing hotel stays with car or train movement also works."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "000000000043",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "000000000042",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "Cruise is convenient, not essential. Trips staying properly in Luxor and Aswan also hold full value."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "000000000045",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "000000000044",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "Think by vacation days"
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "h2"
    },
    {
      "_key": "000000000047",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "000000000046",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "Egypt travel choice varies by days."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "000000000049",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "000000000048",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "One week — narrowing to Cairo and Luxor is realistic. Giza, GEM, part of Cairo, Karnak, Luxor Temple, Valley of the Kings, and major west-bank sites visible."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "00000000004b",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "00000000004a",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "Ten days makes Cairo, Luxor, and Aswan combine easier. Room for Nile cruise or Abu Simbel."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "00000000004d",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "00000000004c",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "Two weeks adds Red Sea, Alexandria, White Desert, or Siwa. No need to include all. Even two weeks isn't enough for all Egypt."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "00000000004f",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "00000000004e",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "As vacation, don't underestimate transfer and rest days. Continuous site days, however wonderful, blur impressions. Inserting museum days, riverside evenings, and seaside rest days makes the trip richer."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "000000000051",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "000000000050",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "For family trips"
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "h2"
    },
    {
      "_key": "000000000053",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "000000000052",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "For Egypt trips with children, trip pace matters more than sight count."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "000000000055",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "000000000054",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "Pyramids, museums, tombs, and temples are strong experiences for children. Heat, transfer, long explanation, and crowds load. Morning one big visit, afternoon rest, evening short walk or light sightseeing is realistic."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "000000000057",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "000000000056",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "In Cairo, don't pack Giza and GEM into the same day. In Luxor, don't add too many Valley of the Kings tombs; choose visually clear places."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "000000000059",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "000000000058",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "Placing Red Sea at the end makes family trips much easier. Pool, sea, short boat trips, and hotel rest receive sightseeing fatigue."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "00000000005b",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "00000000005a",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "Recommended first-trip compositions"
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "h2"
    },
    {
      "_key": "00000000005d",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "00000000005c",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "For first Egypt visitors, these thinkings are usable."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "00000000005f",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "00000000005e",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "Ancient Egypt focus — Cairo, Luxor, Aswan. With margin, Nile cruise or Abu Simbel."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "000000000061",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "000000000060",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "Vacation feel focus — Cairo, Luxor, Red Sea. Combining sites and sea with rest at the end."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "000000000063",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "000000000062",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "City culture interest — longer Cairo stay with Alexandria added."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "000000000065",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "000000000064",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "Nature and landscape focus — consider White Desert or Siwa. On first short trips, consider transfer load."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "000000000067",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "000000000066",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "Luxury trip — invest in hotel, ship, guide, and transfer quality. In Egypt, good guides and well-located hotels greatly set trip quality."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "000000000069",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "000000000068",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "Choose the season"
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "h2"
    },
    {
      "_key": "00000000006b",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "00000000006a",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "Centring on Nile valley and Cairo, October to April is the easiest period. Gentle temperature eases outdoor site walking."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "00000000006d",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "00000000006c",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "December and January have good climate but crowd and cost more. November, February, March balance weather and crowd."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "00000000006f",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "00000000006e",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "May to September brings harsh heat in Luxor and Aswan. In summer, early-morning sites, midday rest, evening movement needed."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "000000000071",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "000000000070",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "Red Sea travels year-round; sea conditions, wind, heat, and resort crowding vary by season. Desert and oases build easier autumn through spring than peak summer."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "000000000073",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "000000000072",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "Practical preparation"
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "h2"
    },
    {
      "_key": "000000000075",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "000000000074",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "Visa requirements vary by nationality and change. Before travel, confirm latest conditions on Egypt's official e-visa site, your country's Egyptian embassy or consulate."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "000000000077",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "000000000076",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "GEM and major-site ticket conditions can change. Popular tombs, special exhibits, supplementary tickets, and photo conditions — confirm on-site or via official information."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "000000000079",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "000000000078",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "Strongly consider travel insurance. Confirm medical fees, trip interruption, delay, baggage, and diving or hot-air-balloon activity coverage."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "00000000007b",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "00000000007a",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "Premise tap water not being drunk; use bottled. In hot seasons, prepare hat, sunscreen, light long sleeve, walking shoes, and oral rehydration."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "00000000007d",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "00000000007c",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "Dress at tourist places is comparatively flexible; at religious sites, covering shoulders and knees fits."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "00000000007f",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "00000000007e",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "Making it an Egypt-like vacation"
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "h2"
    },
    {
      "_key": "000000000081",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "000000000080",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "What matters in Egypt travel isn't including all sights."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "000000000083",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "000000000082",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "Seen only as the pyramid country, Egypt ends as short surprise. Only with temples and tombs, you miss modern city and river life. Only in the Red Sea, you go home without touching world-special historical depth."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "000000000085",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "000000000084",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "The best vacation is a trip centred on your interest, adding a little of another Egypt."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "000000000087",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "000000000086",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "To an archaeology trip, add evening Nile. To a Red Sea vacation, add two Cairo nights. To Cairo city stay, add Alexandria's sea. To a Luxor site trip, add places like Deir el-Medina showing human life."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "000000000089",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "000000000088",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "Egypt isn't a country to finish in one trip. So on first vacations, leaving margin that makes you want to return beats packing all in."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "normal"
    }
  ],
